    "pass": {
      "note": "天驼关: west of 隘口小路 a yellow-stone path runs into woods of grass thirty or forty 尺 high, in fog, to a sunlit clearing with a strange mirror on its north side (the way into the 梦幻迷境, a map of its own). From the 青石官道 (Snow's map) a gravel path runs south-west over the barren clifftop to a half-round mound at the cliff's edge; an iron chain hangs from it seventeen or eighteen 丈 down the rock face to the tail of the 黄石隘口, which the chain is the only way into. The yellow-earth path winds south-west, then south between ever steeper walls; east of it the garrison's camp behind its iron palisade: the gate (two soldiers on duty), the soldiers' tents north and south of it, the camp fire and its well beyond, the squad leaders' tents either side, the vice general's tent, rich with tiger skins and silver, and the general's beyond it. Further south the west wall grows strangely smooth, the wind blows harder by the camp's gate, the iron gate of 天驼关 stands raised over the path with its great winch behind it, and the valley between the two cliffs, shaped like a camel's humps, leads south to 玉螺湖村 (a region of its own).",
